# Correct photographed calibration geometry

## Scope and existing evidence

Historical implementation notes are retained for provenance. The accepted
finite design does not imply unfinished runtime integration exists.

Detect reference marks, perspective, lens distortion, scale, grid, baseline,
and capture quality before treating any observed stroke as evidence.

Current executable evidence now requires one caller-produced observation for
each of those seven photographed-capture geometry families and binds the report
to one stable capture identity. Duplicate families reject in report order and
missing families reject in canonical requirement order; a 128-mask compact
oracle exhausts every presence subset. Successful completeness now also returns
constructor-sealed evidence borrowing the exact report, so later extraction can
require all seven families without treating structural completeness as a quality
pass.

A separate 2,801-sequence oracle covers every axis sequence through length four
and requires the sealed path to preserve duplicate-before-missing precedence
independently. Detection, image decoding, transform
fitting, distortion correction, units/tolerances, capture-quality scoring,
geometry acceptance, and handwriting extraction remain open.

## Finite photographed worksheet geometry and quality contract

**Inputs:** one photograph tied to a captured A4 worksheet identity and
revision, four declared page fiducials, observed pixel positions, camera
orientation and explicit capture-quality evidence. **Outputs:** a proposed
pixel-to-page planar homography in mm, a seven-family geometry report and
quality verdict `Accepted`, `NeedsRecapture`, or `UnsupportedDistortion`.
No stroke extraction may consume a report that is incomplete or refused.

**Reference geometry:** the finite worksheet defines crosses in physical
millimeters at `(15,15)`, `(195,15)`, `(195,282)`, `(15,282)` on a 210 x 297
mm page. Detect each cross with a stable ID, confirm clockwise/non-self-
intersecting order and solve one 3 x 3 projective transform from photo pixel
centers to physical coordinates. Require positive finite scale, stable
inverse and checks against independent known grid/baseline marks; do not use
a guessed nominal DPI. Lens distortion outside a declared camera correction
model cannot be silently absorbed as handwriting deformation.

**Worked example:** a photo has ordered cross centers `(100,100)`,
`(1900,100)`, `(1900,2770)`, `(100,2770)` pixels. For this front-facing ideal
case, 1800 pixels span 180 mm horizontally and 2670 pixels span 267 mm
vertically. The result is 10 pixels/mm with page mapping
`x_mm = 15 + (x_px-100)/10`, `y_mm = 15 + (y_px-100)/10`.
An independent baseline mark at image y=`600` maps to y=`65 mm` as expected.
The seven report families record reference marks, perspective, lens
assumptions, physical scale, grid, baseline and quality, all tied to the same
capture ID. This is a theoretical calibration example, not a detector result.

**Quality policy:** a proposed first-release acceptance threshold is at
least four uniquely matched fiducials, no missing or mirrored corner, a
nondegenerate transform, and independent grid/baseline residual no larger
than 1 mm in physical coordinates. Report blur, shadows, clipping and
reflections as explicit capture observations; if they make stroke boundaries
unreliable, return `NeedsRecapture` despite numerically plausible corners.
Unmodeled barrel/fisheye or rolling-shutter distortion is
`UnsupportedDistortion`, not a corrected stroke sample.

**Refusal example:** repeated top-right mark IDs, only three visible marks,
a folded page, grid residual 2 mm, or severe lens warp refuses geometry
acceptance. Retain raw capture provenance and exact failing condition; do not
invent missing marks, extract paths, change profile style or apply an
unverified image transform to saved handwriting evidence.

**Assumptions and limits:** existing code admits a caller-owned report only
when all seven geometry families are present and no duplicate family exists.
It does not decode photographs, find fiducials, estimate homographies, score
blur or correct a lens. Theoretical acceptance supplies a finite geometric
contract but no functioning calibration photo pipeline or quality proof.

## Acceptance decision

- **Basis:** practical for seven-family report completeness only; theoretical
  for photo detection, transform and quality thresholds, 2026-11-02.
- **Delivered:** four known points, one 10 px/mm worked transform, seven
  required observations, residual threshold and refusal cases.
- **Not implemented by this acceptance:** real camera decoding, fiducial
  detection, homography fitting, lens correction or stroke admission.
